.TH DCINFO 1 "24 Hune 2026" "DICOM PS3" "DICOM PS3 - Summarize information about DICOM file content"
.SH NAME
dcinfo \- ACR/NEMA DICOM PS3 ... DICOM PS3 - Summarize information about DICOM file content
.SH SYNOPSIS
.HP 10
.B dcinfo
.so man1/gen.so
[
.B \-v|verbose
]
[
.B \-filename
]
.so man1/optin.so
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
.B dcinfo
reads the named dicom or acr-nema input file and provides summary information about the content of the composite instance,
such as whether or not it is an image, is multi-frame, is enhanced family, is encapsulated and the presence or absence of
offset tables.
.LP
.SH OPTIONS
The description and verbose output go to standard error.
.PP
The basic input switches are described in dcintro(1). Options specific to this program are:
.TP
.B \-verbose
.RS
Display byte offset from file start and message start, in hexadecimal, and dump contents while reading and once read.
.RE
.TP
.B \-filename
.RS
Show the name of the file supplied in the arguments; a hyphen will be reported if no filename was supplied.
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.LP
\ 
.SH EXAMPLES
.LP
.RE
\ 
.RE
% dcinfo XAImage.dcm
.RE
Transfer Syntax to read data set is encapsulated
.RE
Is a non-enhanced family instance
.RE
Is not an instance of a Concatenation
.RE
Is an image with multiple frames
.RE
Is an image with encapsulated PixelData
.RE
Basic Offset Table is present
.RE
Extended Offset Table is absent
.RE

.RE
% dcinfo WSImage.dcm
.RE
Transfer Syntax to read data set is encapsulated
.RE
Is an enhanced family instance
.RE
Is an enhanced family instance without PerFrameFunctionalGroupsSequence
.RE
Is not an instance of a Concatenation
.RE
Is an image with multiple frames
.RE
Is an image with encapsulated PixelData
.RE
Basic Offset Table is absent
.RE
Extended Offset Table is present
.RE
.SH FILES
.LP
\ 
